About us:
We are a proven boutique Chartered Accountancy firm, providing a wide range of professional services to a dynamic and varied client base. We invest heavily in training and developing our team members in order to provide the highest level of service to our clients. You will be based in a modern office conveniently located just outside the CBD and will be part of an ambitious team with like-minded individuals who strive to succeed and improve.

About the role:
We are seeking an enthusiastic, professional and dynamic Senior Accountant to join our team on a full-time basis. You will be engaging with our diverse client base within the SME environment, offering various business services including taxation, bookkeeping, superannuation and advisory. The role also provides exposure to a broader range of corporate advisory matters as client needs arise, offering scope to develop across the full spectrum of accounting practice.

Duties and responsibilities:
•	Assisting in the management and mentoring of graduate accountants.
•	Preparation of financial statements and tax returns for a wide client base (including SMSFs);
•	Assisting clients with the management of business and tax obligations and lodgement deadlines (including BAS's and IAS's);
•	Providing tax advice to clients across a range of compliance and planning matters;
•	Advising on the tax and ownership structuring considerations that arise from client transactions and business changes;
•	Engaging regularly with clients and maintaining strong relationships;
•	Forecasting tax predictions, understanding the financial landscape and market trends to identify and pre-empt potential tax exposures;
•	Preparing and advising on business management reports to provide insight into the financial performance of clients;
•	Supporting the analysis and valuation of client businesses as part of broader advisory engagements;
•	Preparing the calculations and workpapers that underpin group restructures and consolidations; and
•	Assisting in the management and mentoring of graduate accountants.
Skills and experience
•	Full time;
•	Tertiary Accounting qualifications;
•	CA/CPA qualified or near completion;
•	4+ years' public practice experience;
•	Experience with MYOB, Xero and BGL platforms (CLASS looked favourably upon);
•	Ability to manage SMSF compliance and advisory engagements;
•	Strong technical and communication skills (written and verbal);
•	Comfortable working across a broad advisory scope, including financial analysis and structuring matters as they arise within client engagements; and
•	Able to assist in managing graduate accountants.

What's on offer:
•	Salary range of $90,000 – $120,000. Remuneration will be commensurate with experience;
•	Room to progress to more senior roles;
•	Exposure to a wide variety of clients and industries across compliance and advisory work; and
•	Full CA or CPA support is provided.

Remedial Massage Therapist - Wanted

About Us

Living Winner Pty Ltd (ABN 71 676 335 596)  is a Western Australia–based remedial massage, soft tissue therapy and therapeutic treatment business operating across Perth’s western suburbs. Our business provides professional, assessment-based and outcome-focused therapeutic treatment services to clients experiencing muscular pain, movement restriction, postural tension, sports-related strain, pregnancy-related discomfort, lymphatic concerns, post-exercise recovery needs and other functional soft tissue conditions.

As our business continues to grow, we are seeking a qualified and experienced Remedial Massage Therapist to join our team on a full-time basis.

Your Responsibilities

-  As a Remedial Massage Therapist, you will be expected to provide professional therapeutic treatment services to clients across our business locations, including:
-  Conducting initial client consultations to understand presenting concerns, health history, pain areas, mobility issues, injury history, pregnancy status, recovery needs and treatment goals;
-  Assessing clients’ soft tissue conditions, treatment suitability, contraindications, pressure tolerance and individual treatment requirements;
-  Developing appropriate treatment plans based on each client’s condition, presentation and therapeutic goals;
- Providing remedial massage, deep tissue massage, sports massage, myofascial release, myofascial cupping, manual lymphatic drainage, pregnancy massage and other suitable soft tissue treatment techniques;
-  Providing dry needling therapy where appropriately trained and within professional competency;
-  Modifying treatment techniques, pressure levels and positioning according to client needs, pain tolerance, pregnancy status, recovery stage and relevant health considerations;
-  Assisting clients with muscular pain relief, reduced soft tissue tension, improved range of motion, functional recovery, postural improvement and post-exercise recovery;
-  Taking into account referral notes, care directions or recommendations from medical practitioners, physiotherapists, occupational therapists or other allied health professionals where relevant;
-  Maintaining accurate client treatment notes, treatment plans, aftercare records and business documentation;
-  Providing aftercare guidance, stretching advice, hydration reminders, recovery suggestions and treatment frequency recommendations where appropriate;
-  Maintaining professional hygiene, client safety, privacy and workplace presentation standards;
-  Communicating professionally with clients, team members and business management;
-  Participating in internal practitioner development sessions, case-based discussions and treatment protocol reviews where required;
-  Working across different business or service locations as reasonably required by business A

About You 

The successful candidate will ideally have:

-  A Diploma of Remedial Massage or an equivalent relevant qualification, preferred;
-  Preferably 1–3 years of closely related experience in a remedial massage, therapeutic treatment or recovery environment;
-  Strong skills in client communication, soft tissue assessment, treatment planning and therapeutic treatment delivery;
-  Practical experience in remedial massage, deep tissue treatment, sports massage and myofascial release;
-  Experience or training in myofascial cupping, manual lymphatic drainage, pregnancy massage or dry needling will be highly regarded;
-  Ability to identify contraindications and modify treatment according to each client’s condition, presentation and treatment suitability;
-  Strong communication skills and a client-centred approach to care;
-  Ability to maintain accurate treatment notes and comply with business procedures and treatment protocols;
-  Professional presentation, reliability and commitment to safe treatment practices;
-  Eligibility for provider recognition with relevant private health funds will be highly regarded;
-  Ability to work across multiple business or service locations where required;
-  Commitment to long-term full-time employment and ongoing professional development. 

Who This Role Suits 

This role will suit someone who:

-  Is an experienced Remedial Massage Therapist seeking stable full-time employment;
-  Enjoys working in a professional, therapeutic treatment environment;
-  Has strong interest in pain management, soft tissue recovery, sports recovery, postural tension and functional improvement;
-  Is comfortable working with a broad range of clients, including office workers, sports participants, pregnant clients and clients with chronic muscular tightness or movement restriction;
-  Wants to develop broader practical experience across remedial massage, soft tissue therapy and client-specific treatment planning;
-  Values professional standards, client trust, aftercare and ongoing therapeutic outcomes;
-  Is willing to participate in internal training, case discussions and ongoing professional development.

Why Join Us
-  High growth business with diverse client base. 
-  Attractive compensation $75,000 - $85,000 p.a. plus super
-  Multiple service locations. 
-  Supportive culture.  

If you think this role is for you, please apply with detailed resume.
